-- Clean-start additive organization schema (Plan B Task 1).
--
-- The DDL portion was generated by diffing the LIVE fresh dev database
-- (app_cleanstart_dev, created by `prisma db push` of the prior schema) against
-- the new datamodel:
--   npx prisma migrate diff \
--     --from-url "$DATABASE_URL" \
--     --to-schema-datamodel prisma/schema.prisma \
--     --script
-- and is followed by the partial unique indexes Prisma cannot express.
--
-- ADDITIVE ONLY: no legacy model, column, enum, or index is dropped or
-- altered destructively here. Legacy structures stay until the B15 schema
-- finalization task squashes this migration into the single canonical
-- `00000000000001_clean_start_init` initial migration.
--
-- Applying this migration is a controlled release operation: this file is the
-- contract artifact; the fresh dev database is synchronized with `prisma db
-- push` (additions only, never --accept-data-loss, never reset). The four
-- partial unique indexes below are SQL-contract-only locally and are exercised
-- for real in the disposable CI database by the B13 integration suite.
--
-- Circular FK note: organization_assignments.teamId -> teams (SET NULL) and
-- teams.reportsToAssignmentId -> organization_assignments (RESTRICT) are both
-- added AFTER both tables exist, in that order.
--
-- Snapshot-constraint notes (audited): every new position reference uses
-- RESTRICT so referenced positions can never be hard-deleted (deactivation is
-- the removal path); the restart self-relation on approval_instances preserves
-- the superseded attempt row; approval_candidate_group_members.capturedDisplayName
-- stays required (labels frozen at capture).

